    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114595" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρεωκοπ-ίδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who cancels his debts, an insolvent</i>: esp. said of
			those friends of Solon at Athens, who took advantage of his <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σεισάχθεια,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sol.</u>
				15
			</span></i>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρεώκοπ-ος</span></b>  (parox.), ὁ, =
			<i>creditor, decoctor,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρεο-</span>).</div>
